> Servings: 5

= Ingredients

@(14- to 15-oz) can cannellini beans, rinsed and drained{1 1/4}\
@garlic cloves, finely chopped{2 1/2}\
@fresh lemon juice{1 1/4%tablespoon}\
@olive oil{2 1/2%tablespoons}\
@chopped fresh flat-leaf parsley or basil{2 1/2%tablespoons}\
@salt{3/8%teaspoon}\
@black pepper{3/8%teaspoon}\
@(6-oz) cans Italian tuna in oil, drained{2 1/2}\
@finely chopped fresh basil or flat-leaf parsley{2 1/2%tablespoons}\
@pitted Kalamata or other brine-cured black olives, finely chopped{3/8%cup}\
@celery rib, finely chopped{1 1/4}\
@finely chopped red onion{2 1/2%tablespoons}\
@olive oil{2 1/2%tablespoons}\
@fresh lemon juice{1 1/4%tablespoon}\
@salt{3/8%teaspoon}\
@black pepper{1/8%teaspoon}\
@(1/3-inch-thick) slices rustic Italian bread (from a round crusty loaf) or 4 (4-inch-long) oval panini rolls{10}\
@loosely packed trimmed watercress sprigs{1 1/4%cup}

= Directions
Coarsely mash beans with a fork in a bowl, then stir in garlic, lemon juice, oil, parsley, salt, and pepper.

Flake tuna in a bowl with a fork, then stir in basil, olives, celery, onion, oil, lemon juice, salt, and pepper until combined.

Spoon one fourth of bean mixture on 1 slice of bread, then top with one fourth of tuna salad, some watercress, and a slice of bread. Make 3 more sandwiches in same manner.
